 "question": "What does the build cylinder fit into?",
 "before": {
  "answer": "The build cylinder fits around the build base: the BOM says the base should be about 1 mm smaller in radius, and the drawings give the cylinder’s inside diameter as Ø252 and the base’s outside diameter as Ø250 [BOM.47.design_intent] [BOM.46.design_intent] [D-023.p1.vision.c10] [D-024.p1.a08]. A ceramic seal sits in the base’s groove against the cylinder wall [Zaxis_legend.l07] [Zaxis_legend.l06].\n\nCaution: the cylinder drawing is a degraded scan, and its Ø262,0 and Ø264,0 H7 callouts failed the ISO 286 check; no fit relation is inferred from those readings [D-023.p1.vision.c06] [D-023.p1.vision.c07].",
