 "after": {
  "answer": "The build cylinder appears to fit into the **Main Platform**: the cylinder’s corrected Ø262,0 j7 diameter matches the platform’s Ø262 H8 bore. This is an **inferred** transition fit from the drawings; no source explicitly says they mate. [D-023.p1.vision.c06.C-001] [D-003.p1.vision.c15]\n\nSeparately, the system diagram says the cylinder **registers on the Print Platform** at its top edge. [Zaxis_legend.l03] [Zaxis_legend.l04]\n\nThere is also a Ø264,0 H7 callout on the cylinder drawing, but its tolerance failed an ISO 286 check, so it should not be relied on for identifying a fit. [D-023.p1.vision.c07]",
